     vvddeevvpprrooppss — native and user-defined properties of ZFS vdevs

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Properties are divided into two types, native properties and user-defined
     (or "user") properties.  Native properties either export internal statis‐
     tics or control ZFS behavior.  In addition, native properties are either
     editable or read-only.  User properties have no effect on ZFS behavior,
     but you can use them to annotate vdevs in a way that is meaningful in
     your environment.  For more information about user properties, see the
     _U_s_e_r _P_r_o_p_e_r_t_i_e_s section, below.

   NNaattiivvee PPrrooppeerrttiieess
     Every vdev has a set of properties that export statistics about the vdev
     as well as control various behaviors.  Properties are not inherited from
     top-level vdevs, with the exception of checksum_n, checksum_t, io_n,
     io_t, slow_io_n, and slow_io_t.

     The values of numeric properties can be specified using human-readable
     suffixes (for example, kk, KKBB, MM, GGbb, and so forth, up to ZZ for
     zettabyte).  The following are all valid (and equal) specifications:
     1536M, 1.5g, 1.50GB.

     The values of non-numeric properties are case sensitive and must be low‐
     ercase.

